{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T10:45:06.257Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5a19c20da0d320085dc6f794","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-04T10:45:06.256Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"CI correction: exact-head CI failed the Duplication gate with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND 'fast-glob' imported from pm-ops/dist/duplication.js. Root cause: pm-ops declares fast-glob as an OPTIONAL peer, but its duplication gate hard-requires it at runtime; this repo's direct fast-glob devDependency exists precisely to satisfy that peer, so removing it broke the gate while my earlier local gate passed only against a stale node_modules (npm install had not pruned it at that point; npm ci is authoritative). fast-glob ^3.3.3 restored; npm ci + full npm run release:check PASS again (duplication-gate 0/9209 lines, 27 sources, 0 clone pairs at threshold 0%). npm audit now reports the same pre-existing dev-only braces (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm) chain that origin/main also reports (main: 7 high; this branch: 4 high - the eslint 10.12/jscpd 5.4 upgrades shrink it), with no patched braces version published, so it is unfixable in-tree without breaking the pm-ops gate; npm audit --omit=dev remains 0 vulnerabilities, which is the gate this repo enforces. Upstream defect to file: pm-ops's fast-glob peer is not actually optional."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T10:45:06.257Z"}],"before_hash":"a91587dd5d0a2afe51d8a74f032ce024f1fb0c03941c5c9bdce6e25be8d01a97","after_hash":"af89d1c7a6d8490a3a813864bf749a10da5f1984c5d05ca1308166718893b3cb","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4d06c6ad90917dae58c742dc0637227ccc05453437151860b62b8f229005a40a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T10:45:14.726Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5a19c20da0d320085dc6f794","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Pins raised: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.4 (exact), pm-ops 2026.10.4, pm-changelog 2026.9.25, jscpd ^5.4.0; codeql-action SHA group 2892aa5; fast-glob ^3.3.3 retained because pm-ops's duplication gate hard-requires it (optional-peer defect reproduced in CI: ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND; fixed by restoring it). Carried #122's zero-dup fixes and pm item pm-gantt-chart-chso with its history chain re-anchored (history_drift health finding cleared). npm audit --omit=dev: 0 vulnerabilities; full npm audit carries only the same pre-existing unfixable dev-only braces chain as main (4 vs main's 7 high - reduced by this PR's upgrades; no patched braces version exists). npm ci + full npm run release:check PASS with unchanged zero-duplication gate and coverage thresholds; accept:packed green on hosts 2026.10.4 and 2026.8.20. npx pm health exit 0. Real-tracker dogfood via npx and bunx passed (gantt render, group-by, json/svg export). pm-github 2026.10.4 managed extension with read-only previews only."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T10:45:14.726Z"}],"before_hash":"af89d1c7a6d8490a3a813864bf749a10da5f1984c5d05ca1308166718893b3cb","after_hash":"1241a40c52685bd3796268aaae3b01ad26ca05aee23e24b3440e377d6448009d","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7896263325e29045a4a2758385e81383c90891d281e6ad3b38a1790cd0f860b8"}
